{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "takeId": "formal-take-01",
  "seconds": 290,
  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 6.585365853658536,
      "text": "Mandate Wallet lets an AI agent purchase an approved API service within an owner-defined budget.",
      "chapter": "purpose"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.585365853658536,
      "end": 14.048780487804878,
      "text": "We will connect it to Claude Desktop, obtain an ETH statistics sample, and produce a short brief.",
      "chapter": "purpose"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.048780487804878,
      "end": 18,
      "text": "The transactions in this demonstration run on Base Sepolia.",
      "chapter": "purpose"
    },
    {
      "start": 18,
      "end": 26.0,
      "text": "Prepare Claude Desktop, Rabby and Node twenty-four, then start Mandate using the manual’s setup command.",
      "chapter": "prerequisites"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.0,
      "end": 34,
      "text": "The owner needs test ETH and USDC. This demo uses controlled services and fixed statistics.",
      "chapter": "prerequisites"
    },
    {
      "start": 34,
      "end": 43.411764705882355,
      "text": "Choose Testnet and Base Sepolia in the setup wizard. Connect the owner wallet, then review deployment,",
      "chapter": "public-setup"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.411764705882355,
      "end": 55.1764705882353,
      "text": "funding and permissions. We transfer zero point one five test USDC to the smart account and fund operator gas separately.",
      "chapter": "public-setup"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.1764705882353,
      "end": 64.58823529411765,
      "text": "The task budget is zero point one five, each payment is capped at zero point one,",
      "chapter": "public-setup"
    },
    {
      "start": 64.58823529411765,
      "end": 74,
      "text": "and the session expires after two hours. The owner confirms these transactions in the external wallet.",
      "chapter": "public-setup"
    },
    {
      "start": 74,
      "end": 81.57894736842105,
      "text": "After confirmation, open the authorization transaction in BaseScan. Check the Base Sepolia network, transaction hash and successful receipt.",
      "chapter": "grant-explorer"
    },
    {
      "start": 81.57894736842105,
      "end": 90,
      "text": "The contract log links the session to the approved mandate. The complete hash will also appear in our execution evidence.",
      "chapter": "grant-explorer"
    },
    {
      "start": 90,
      "end": 100.65217391304348,
      "text": "Download the Guided package for this Base Sepolia configuration. In Claude Desktop, open Settings,",
      "chapter": "claude-install"
    },
    {
      "start": 100.65217391304348,
      "end": 112.82608695652175,
      "text": "Extensions and Advanced settings, then import and enable the package. Its local connection is already configured,",
      "chapter": "claude-install"
    },
    {
      "start": 112.82608695652175,
      "end": 125,
      "text": "so no Agent profile or Connection file is selected. Start a new conversation using this connection.",
      "chapter": "claude-install"
    },
    {
      "start": 125,
      "end": 132.85714285714286,
      "text": "Ask Claude to read the account context and quote the approved ETH sample without purchasing.",
      "chapter": "context-quote"
    },
    {
      "start": 132.85714285714286,
      "end": 142.28571428571428,
      "text": "Check the chain, account, active session and remaining budget. The sample costs zero point zero one test USDC.",
      "chapter": "context-quote"
    },
    {
      "start": 142.28571428571428,
      "end": 147,
      "text": "Installing the connector does not expand the approved authority.",
      "chapter": "context-quote"
    },
    {
      "start": 147,
      "end": 160.75,
      "text": "Authorize the quoted purchase. Mandate registers the commitment before releasing a payment signature. The USDC transfer settles on Base Sepolia,",
      "chapter": "purchase"
    },
    {
      "start": 160.75,
      "end": 172.4375,
      "text": "but our controlled service deliberately fails its first response. Claude reports payment, delivery and result validation separately.",
      "chapter": "purchase"
    },
    {
      "start": 172.4375,
      "end": 180,
      "text": "A successful payment alone does not mean the data was delivered.",
      "chapter": "purchase"
    },
    {
      "start": 180,
      "end": 189.56521739130434,
      "text": "Open the settlement transaction in BaseScan. Check Success, the test USDC contract, and the ERC-twenty transfer from the smart account",
      "chapter": "payment-explorer"
    },
    {
      "start": 189.56521739130434,
      "end": 198.65217391304347,
      "text": "to the approved recipient for zero point zero one USDC. The transaction sender may be the facilitator paying gas;",
      "chapter": "payment-explorer"
    },
    {
      "start": 198.65217391304347,
      "end": 202,
      "text": "the token-transfer sender identifies the paying account.",
      "chapter": "payment-explorer"
    },
    {
      "start": 202,
      "end": 212.08163265306123,
      "text": "Claude resumes the same ETH step after checking its payment state. The original order and settlement hash are retained,",
      "chapter": "recover-brief"
    },
    {
      "start": 212.08163265306123,
      "end": 221.10204081632654,
      "text": "and there is no second payment. The service returns the sample and the result checker validates it.",
      "chapter": "recover-brief"
    },
    {
      "start": 221.10204081632654,
      "end": 228,
      "text": "Claude writes a brief, identifies the fixed demonstration dataset, and cites the settlement.",
      "chapter": "recover-brief"
    },
    {
      "start": 228,
      "end": 237.15384615384616,
      "text": "Claude prepares a revocation request. The owner reviews it in the wallet workspace and signs in Rabby.",
      "chapter": "revoke-explorer"
    },
    {
      "start": 237.15384615384616,
      "end": 247.92307692307693,
      "text": "The BaseScan receipt and SessionRevoked log confirm the change. Future spending by this session is blocked while the completed purchase",
      "chapter": "revoke-explorer"
    },
    {
      "start": 247.92307692307693,
      "end": 249,
      "text": "remains recorded.",
      "chapter": "revoke-explorer"
    },
    {
      "start": 249,
      "end": 258.27272727272725,
      "text": "Finally, ask Claude to attempt the unused BTC sample. The revoked session prevents a new payment registration.",
      "chapter": "refusal"
    },
    {
      "start": 258.27272727272725,
      "end": 268.09090909090907,
      "text": "This refusal has no new transaction hash because it is stopped before broadcast. We retain the tool result,",
      "chapter": "refusal"
    },
    {
      "start": 268.09090909090907,
      "end": 273,
      "text": "permission state and unchanged payment records as refusal evidence.",
      "chapter": "refusal"
    },
    {
      "start": 273,
      "end": 280.0833333333333,
      "text": "The evidence package connects each recorded step to its transaction, contract events and service outcome.",
      "chapter": "close"
    },
    {
      "start": 280.0833333333333,
      "end": 289.52777777777777,
      "text": "Payment and service delivery are documented separately. A local practice option is also available for learning the workflow without public-testnet",
      "chapter": "close"
    },
    {
      "start": 289.52777777777777,
      "end": 290,
      "text": "funds.",
      "chapter": "close"
    }
  ],
